# RTT_Showcase.umap — Scene Manifest  
**RTT / Integrations / UE6 / Maps**

A curated UE6 map demonstrating RTT operators in real time.

---

## Map Name
`RTT_Showcase.umap`

## Purpose
Provide a single scene where students and developers can observe:

- φ emergence fields  
- variance stabilization  
- resonance propagation  
- entropy boundaries  
- hybrid operator behavior  

---

## Scene Layout

```
RTT_Showcase
    ├── Area_PhiField
    │       └── BP_RTT_Primitives (phi demo)
    ├── Area_Variance
    │       └── BP_RTT_Primitives (variance demo)
    ├── Area_Resonance
    │       └── BP_RTT_ResonanceDemo
    ├── Area_Entropy
    │       └── BP_RTT_EntropyDemo
    ├── Area_Hybrid
    │       └── BP_RTT_HybridDemo
    └── UI
            └── WBP_RTT_OperatorPanel (runtime)
```

---

## Actors

| Actor | Purpose |
|-------|---------|
| `BP_RTT_Primitives` | φ + variance baseline |
| `BP_RTT_ResonanceDemo` | resonance visualization |
| `BP_RTT_EntropyDemo` | entropy field visualization |
| `BP_RTT_HybridDemo` | hybrid operator showcase |
| `DirectionalLight` | stable lighting |
| `SkyAtmosphere` | consistent environment |
| `PlayerStart` | runtime entry point |

---

## Editor Tools Integration
- `RTTTools.py` available in toolbar  
- Resonance + entropy visualizers work in‑editor  
- Operator timeline can be opened during PIE  

---

## Status
Ready for implementation.  
Fully aligned with the 2026 RTT Integrations standard.
